{"id":"460167534","kind":"article","title":"认知革命","author":"Andy Matuschak","original_authors":["Andy Matuschak"],"original_source_urls":["https://notes.andymatuschak.org/The_cognitive_revolution"],"publisher":"Thoughts Memo","column":"认知基石 & 教育培训","date":"2022-01-21","updated":"2025-07-11","votes":21,"comment_count":3,"minutes":2,"chars":723,"keywords":["认知革命","行为主义","认知心理学","认知主义","记忆"],"summary":"短文概述认知革命如何挑战行为主义：Tolman 的迷宫实验、Chomsky 对 Skinner 语言理论的批评及 Bartlett 的图式研究，都显示记忆、信念等内在过程对解释行为不可或缺。借助计算机的信息处理类比，心理学逐渐形成认知心理学与认知主义框架。","zhihu_url":"https://zhuanlan.zhihu.com/p/460167534","restoration":null,"toc":[{"id":"sec-1","level":2,"title":"促成认知革命的关键因素"},{"id":"sec-2","level":2,"title":"链接至本文"},{"id":"sec-3","level":2,"title":"声明"}],"html":"<p data-pid=\"pUwIKIi2\">{二十世纪中叶}，许多学者指出了<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/zGYJ27hxJfdLQHBWedUpD5sq3p9Y1GnKk9q\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">行为主义</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-1\"><a href=\"#ref-1\">[1]</a></sup>的局限性：行为依赖于{不可观测到的内在现象}，如{记忆和信念}等。行为主义者认为{这些现象是主观的}，而不将其纳入实验中。</p><p data-pid=\"qWR5XT6O\">心理学家开始研究这些内在现象。他们使用了<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z4EhH4wm5Lw5rhF2omcLxvmFT7SnnmH1v7kd4\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">超验方法</a>和借鉴自计算机科学的思想，最终发展出<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/zLQzZhPX1oCXyCAt6fL1J2Hf6vWnEw91jhz\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">认知心理学</a>，并奠定了<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z29ws8NQEBoinKywNv2fx74PJ32CQm96uhau\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">认知主义</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-2\"><a href=\"#ref-2\">[2]</a></sup>的理论框架。</p><h2 id=\"sec-1\">促成认知革命的关键因素</h2><p data-pid=\"1bHYIEvR\">1948 年，{Edward Tolman} 大鼠实验证明了{知识}在行为中的作用。他{让大鼠探索迷宫数天}，之后{在迷宫中放置食物}，来测试它们。他观察到{大鼠能够立即找到迷宫中的食物}，这表明它们已经习得了「{认知地图}」。然而<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/zGYJ27hxJfdLQHBWedUpD5sq3p9Y1GnKk9q\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">行为主义</a>的理论中，学习被理解为{行为变化}，这难以解释这种现象。</p><p data-pid=\"GT8DGuRh\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/zv4siQE8YmE7gU1tcoeQV4H9SEnrkAahyby\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">B. F. Skinner</a> 的著作《言语行为》(1957年) 主张语言可以通过{<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z151kK7wBFk9U6tVXGzxTxignvwfKtAaAK1\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">操作性条件反射</a>}学习。{<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z4SLQdjLRfsiAfpXJt3JYVMum23Pr4jthji6F\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Noam Chomsky</a>} 发表了一篇尖锐的批判，指出{孩童能说出的一些言语，是孩子从未听过，或者从未因此而受奖赏过的}。</p><p data-pid=\"i9IhjuDC\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/zWA26zctXTTLEQ1ikD4KuqTC4ffizupyo4XX\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Frederic Bartlett</a> 的实验表明，人们通过他称之为「图式」的心理框架来解释他们的经历。</p><p data-pid=\"KZHGLACJ\">计算机技术激荡起一波心理学理论的新浪潮，其中应用了很多信息加工的引喻：如缓冲区、门、事件加工等等。</p><p data-pid=\"02p5vz0s\">问：<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/Transcendental_method\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">超验方法</a>对<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/Cognitive_psychology\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">认知心理学</a>的意义是什么？<br/>答：它解决了一个重要的悖论：理解行为必须去理解内在现象，然而内在现象无法直接观测到。</p><h2 id=\"sec-2\">链接至本文</h2><ul><li data-pid=\"NDNnnlJF\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"696291865\" href=\"#/post/696291865\">认知主义</a></li><li data-pid=\"o1uqeeNp\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"1926940228100268129\" href=\"#/post/1926940228100268129\">行为主义</a></li></ul><h2 id=\"sec-3\">声明</h2><p data-pid=\"EXe-X8pe\">此内容发布由 Andy Matuschak 许可。未经允许，不得转载或修改。保留所有权利。</p><p class=\"ztext-empty-paragraph\"><br/></p><blockquote data-pid=\"yvZejQAO\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://paratranz.cn/projects/3131\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Thoughts Memo</a> 汉化组译制<br/>原文：<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/The_cognitive_revolution\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">The cognitive revolution</a></blockquote><hr/><ol class=\"references\"><li id=\"ref-1\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-1\">↩</a> 行为主义 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"1926940228100268129\" href=\"#/post/1926940228100268129\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-2\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-2\">↩</a> 认知主义 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"696291865\" href=\"#/post/696291865\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li></ol>","rec_chain":[{"id":"459716066","title":"好的练习包含更有效的组块重新编码方案","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":13,"minutes":2,"reason":"同专栏上一篇 · 认知基石 & 教育培训"},{"id":"461578699","title":"人类作为信息处理机时的“信道容量”","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":16,"minutes":3,"reason":"同专栏下一篇 · 认知基石 & 教育培训"},{"id":"1926940228100268129","title":"行为主义","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":15,"minutes":1,"reason":"本文直接引用"},{"id":"696291865","title":"认知主义","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":16,"minutes":2,"reason":"本文直接引用"}],"rec_bridge":[{"id":"1979480219023869096","title":"想入场？你起码得读过一本书。","author":"Ludicity","votes":262,"minutes":16,"reason":"跨学派视角 · Ludicity"},{"id":"564164660","title":"杏仁体可能涉及到奖励新奇的输入","author":"Edmund T. Rolls","votes":6,"minutes":1,"reason":"跨学派视角 · Edmund T. Rolls"},{"id":"562035095","title":"感受学习乐趣的过程涉及到阿片受体","author":"Irving Biederman","votes":8,"minutes":1,"reason":"跨作者共鸣「记忆」· Irving Biederman"}],"rec_answers":[]}